    "created_at": "2016-03-11T10:51:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-11T10:51:12Z",
    "body": "So it seems like the solution here is to remove the \"alias\" concept and instead just directly set the origin member to an already allocated origin. That way a single origin would be shared by multiple parties.\n\n@mikewest does @bzbarsky's understanding of Chrome match yours?\n\n(I don't really know if the HTML standard is trying to avoid letting blob/about/javascript/srcdoc control their parent effective script origin. It does not seem super important if it's not implemented.)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
