    "created_at": "2016-03-11T14:44:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-11T14:44:11Z",
    "body": "hum, while we set the domain to the potentially aliased origin directly, we only propagate the new origin to the script context that set it. If we don't unalias, this would require setting the new domain in all script contexts that share the security origin.\n\nShouldn't we rather fix the implementations here?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
