    "created_at": "2016-03-11T14:55:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-11T14:55:21Z",
    "body": "Fix them to what behavior?  Again, current spec has this weird asymmetry where setting domain on the parent will propagate it to the child, but not vice versa.  No one implements that right now, and it's not clear to me that it's in any way desirable.\n\nAnyway, I'm having a hard time reconciling https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/794#issuecomment-195395293 with the actual experimental results of https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/794#issue-138270770 -- I don't know what the code _thinks_ it's doing, but the upshot is that after it runs something that has set .domain is same-effective-script-origin with something that \"has not set it\" (in Blink).\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
