    "created_at": "2016-03-11T14:58:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-11T14:58:12Z",
    "body": "in blink, we have two places where we store the origin: in the script context and on the document. If the domain in the script context doesn't match, we fall back to comparing the one from the document. So here, I guess what happens is that there's a mismatch in the script, so we fall back to comparing the document's origin, and they match for both frames because we didn't un-alias them.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
